  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 27

Iteration 26 named this wider run. This file takes it.

Do not overwrite 04-26.

## What ran

Full amu `test-runner` suite (138 namespaces), twice on judah,
worktree `/tmp/amu-iter27`, amu `f21f5c9f` (includes the iteration-26
spill fixture). ~70s each arm.

Production (no override):

- 1098 tests, 7441 pass, 0 fail, 87 error

Override `mir/back-edge?` => false (`OVERRIDE_CALLS` 1219, live):

- 1098 tests, 7437 pass, 4 fail, 87 error

The four FAILs are the only delta, all production all-vreg policy
assertions on the two GMIR fixtures:

- `a-call-and-a-back-edge-across-a-spill-execute` aarch64: expected
  `:all-vregs` actual `:call-live`
- same x86-64
- `a-call-and-a-back-edge-in-one-function-execute` aarch64: expected
  `[:all-vregs 8]` actual `[:call-live 0]`
- same x86-64

Pass count dropped by exactly 4. The 87 errors are identical to
baseline (`wasm-tools`/`wasmtime` missing on judah + 3 cli status 70).
They are not caused by the override.

This file does **not** remove `back-edge?`. Removal is a kotoba-mir
change plus rewriting those 4 asserts (and mir's
`v3-call-plus-back-edge-is-routed-to-all-vregs`).

Green-both-ways was avoided by `OVERRIDE_CALLS` 1219 and by the 4
policy fails: if the override had not applied, those asserts would
still be all-vreg.

## What this is not

Not predicate removal. The suite executes with the scanner path except
the four production policy asserts that *name* the guard. That is
evidence for a later removal, not the removal.

Not cfg-liveness. Allocator code is unchanged (`ac14016d` / `69e364e`).
deps.edn was not bumped. kotoba-mir and kotoba-native were not moved.

Not a claim that judah's 87 errors are an override regression. They
are the baseline on this machine. Iteration 21's 1096/8235/0 was a
machine with wasm-tools; this measurement is not that one.

## Pins

- amu `f21f5c9f880672b34ed0384c257e892ba0288d62`
  west-pin `08cc6ad5d0c67fd4948d70ec202e40cbb2c523de`
- kotoba-mir not moved (`6ccc30eb4a90548c94bc62a912e91386197a069e`,
  west-pin `0501c1bdd47159c4045630eb0d297ab1b1b384ec`)
- kotoba-native not moved (`69e364edf3154aa8fdf7d87535ca73179b4d2716`)

## Meta-review

- **The remaining hole after 26 was not \"scanner miscompiles other
  amu programs when back-edge? is false\".** The only new fails are
  the four production all-vreg policy assertions.
- **Keep the production assertion when the override goes green.** The
  four fails are those asserts firing, which is how we know the
  override applied to the fixtures that encode the contract.
- **Do not treat 87 errors as an override signal.** They are present
  in both arms.

## Next

Remove `back-edge?` (and update the production all-vreg asserts)
against this evidence, or keep it. `:cfg-liveness` is still false and
is not this week's work. kotoba-mir / kotoba-native still do not
execute compiled programs.

Do not chase fused-srem, extra MOV, FMA, PGO, kototama optimizer, a
timed `bench` export, or rematching leaf vs LLVM. Do not overwrite
04-26. Do not claim LLVM beaten. Do not remove `back-edge?` in this
file. Do not implement cfg-liveness as a drive-by of this suite."}]
